{
  "name": "What to Expect During a Full Kitchen Gut Renovation",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "A full kitchen gut renovation is a serious undertaking, but the results can be absolutely transformative! When you commit to a \"gut job,\" you're essentially stripping the kitchen down to its bones to rebuild it exactly how you envision. The initial phase is all about design and planning – you'll work with a pro to finalize layout changes, material selections, and appliance choices. This part is crucial, as any changes later can cause significant delays and costs. Next comes demolition, which can be messy and loud but also quite satisfying as you see the old space disappear. Then, structural and mechanical work begins. This is when new walls might go up, and plumbing and electrical lines are moved or updated. Remember, permits and inspections are often a must for these types of changes, so your contractor should be handling those details. Finally, it’s all about the finishes: cabinets, countertops, flooring, painting, and appliance installation. The timeline for a full gut renovation can vary, but generally, you're looking at around 18-20 weeks from start to finish. HH Remodeling LLC specializes in these full-scope renovations, and Abraham, as the hands-on owner, ensures everything runs smoothly, even coordinating sub-trades for the specialized plumbing and electrical work. It’s a big project, but with the right team, it’s definitely worth it!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
